  },
  "e998c73d-30f9-4d3d-8a3c-1df1ece9e887": {
   "kind": "theory-wording",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p28-projection-definition",
     "replacement": "$\\operatorname{proj}_{\\underset{\\sim}{b}}\\underset{\\sim}{a}$ is a **vector**.\n\n$\\operatorname{proj}_{\\underset{\\sim}{b}}\\underset{\\sim}{a}$ means the **projection** of $\\underset{\\sim}{a}$ onto $\\underset{\\sim}{b}$.\n\nIt is the “shadow” of $\\underset{\\sim}{a}$ cast onto the line containing $\\underset{\\sim}{b}$.\n\nIt is the component of $\\underset{\\sim}{a}$ parallel to $\\underset{\\sim}{b}$.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p28-projection-definition",
     "targetFingerprint": "91e1fece302e84facaad147d57ad6b0c88a31913b060ee656eefc357d695fbd0",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6ext1-2-further-operations-with-vectors-v1/20261111-121852",
   "revision": 14
  },
  "d32c6d81-91d3-4e2d-8aff-071837592c6d": {
   "kind": "theory-wording",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p28-projection-formula",
     "replacement": "Use the formula below to calculate $\\operatorname{proj}_{\\underset{\\sim}{b}}\\underset{\\sim}{a}$.\n\nFor $\\underset{\\sim}{b}\\ne\\underset{\\sim}{0}$,\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{proj}_{\\underset{\\sim}{b}}\\underset{\\sim}{a}&=\\left(\\frac{\\underset{\\sim}{a}\\cdot\\underset{\\sim}{b}}{|\\underset{\\sim}{b}|^2}\\right)\\underset{\\sim}{b}\\\\&=(\\underset{\\sim}{a}\\cdot\\hat{b})\\hat{b}\\qquad\\text{using }\\hat{b}=\\frac{\\underset{\\sim}{b}}{|\\underset{\\sim}{b}|}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nColumn notation is generally neater when working with vector projections.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p28-projection-formula",
     "targetFingerprint": "3717faae0cde40488a2d75eeb0365307f15eb5b9766d01bc866898bb6f230c0e",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6ext1-2-further-operations-with-vectors-v1/20261111-121852",
   "revision": 14
  },
  "7d8c1c4f-0ca8-4c64-be54-80a659c80c0e": {
   "kind": "theory-definition",
   "payloads": [
    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p30-perpendicular-introduction",
     "replacement": "To find the **component of $\\underline{a}$ perpendicular to $\\underline{b}$** (where $\\underline{b}\\ne\\underline{0}$), subtract the projection from $\\underline{a}$:\n\n$\\text{Perpendicular component}=\\underline{a}-\\operatorname{proj}_{\\underline{b}}\\underline{a}$",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p30-perpendicular-introduction",
